ter 3rd read above\nhas requested the Government to remove the additional 2% tax levied on\nSecond or more personalized vehicles upto a seating capacity of ten (10) in all\nowned by an individual at the time of registration of new vehicles, by suitably\namending the Seventh Schedule of the Telangana Motor vehicles Taxation\nAct, 1963 for facilitating smooth migration to the VAHAN (NIC) application.\n2. Government after careful examination, hereby decided to remove the\nadditional 2% tax levied on Second or more personalized vehicles upto a\nseating capacity of ten (10) in all owned by an individual at the time of\nregistration of new vehicles, by suitably amending the Seventh Schedule to\nthe Telangana Motor vehicles Taxation Act, 1963(Act No.5 of 1963).\n3. Accordingly, the following notification shall be published in an\nextraordinary issue of the Telangana Gazette, dated:23.03.2026.\nNOTIFICATION\nIn exercise of the powers conferred by section 17 of the Telangana\nMotor Vehicles Taxation Act, 1963(Act No.5 of 1963), the Government of\nTelangana hereby issue the following amendment to the Seventh Schedule\nunder section 3 of the Telangana Motor Vehicles Taxation Act, 1963, as\namended from time to time.\nAMENDMENT\nIn the said Act;- in the Seventh Schedule in Section 3 there under, the\ncolumn No.8, and the entries relating thereto i.e. Second or more\npersonalized vehicles upto a seating capacity of ten (10) in all owned by an\nindividual (Additional 2% of tax on the rates prescribed in the Third Schedule\nand Sixth Schedule at the time of registration of new vehicles only) shall be\ndeleted.\n(PTO)\n- 2 -\n4. This notification shall come into force with effect from 23.03.2026\n(BY ORDER AND IN THE NAME OF THE GOVERNOR OF TELANGANA)\nVIKAS RAJ\nSPECIAL CHIEF SECRETARY TO GOVERNMENT\nTo\nThe Commissioner of Printing Stationery & Stores Purchase,Chenchalguda,\nHyderabad. (He is requested to publish the notification in the Extra-Ordinary\nissue of the Telangana Gazette, dated:23.03.2026 and send 200 Copies to the\nTransport Commissioner, Hyderabad and (50) copies to Government.\nThe Transport Commissioner, Telangana State, Hyderabad.\nThe Director General of Police, Hyderabad.\nThe Commissioner of Police, Hyderabad.\nAll the Officers in Transport Department (through the Transport\nCommissioner, Hyderabad).\nThe Director of information & Public Relations, Hyderabad.\nThe Accountant General, Telangana, Hyderabad.\nThe GA(GPM & AR) Department, Secretariat, Hyderabad.\nCopy to:\nThe Law (C) Department.\nThe PS to Principal Secretary to Hon’ble Chief Minister.\nThe OSD to Hon’ble Minister (Transport & BCW).\nThe PS to Special Chief Secretary to Govt., TR&B Department.\nSF/SC.\n// FORWARDED:: BY ORDER//\nSECTION OFFICER", "metadata": {"parts": 1, "source_url": "https://goir.telangana.gov.in/", "sha256": "139f96454954a4b77b3f07a796946827c29a81754f9a782e3e25dd5dfc76e0d5", "provision_heading": "under section 3 of Telangana Motor Vehicles Taxation", "issuing_authority": "Transport, Roads & Buildings (Tr.I) Department, Government of Telangana", "page_end": 2, "verification_status": "unverified", "page_start": 1, "extraction_warning": "Amends G.O.Ms.No. 53/2025's Seventh Schedule (deletes column 8). Effective date and scope taken from the G.O. text only; gazette print not held. Not used for answers until independently reviewed.", "has_table": false, "part": 1, "source_class": "official", "chapter": "", "jurisdiction": "Telangana", "manifest_id": "go-ms-16-2026-trb", "split_method": "whole", "publication_date": "", "state": "Telangana", "document_number": "G.O.Ms.No. 16", "answer_eligible": false, "provision_kind": "Schedule", "effective_date": "", "title": "Amendment to the Seventh Schedule under section 3 of Telangana Motor Vehicles Taxation Act, 1963 (Act No.5 of 1963) - Notification", "source_file": "2026TRB_Ms16.pdf", "validity_status": "unknown", "manifest_notes": "Department G.O. copy dated 20-03-2026, from the GOIR register. Amends the Seventh Schedule as amended by G.O.Ms.No. 22/2022 and 53/2025 (removes the additional 2% tax on second or more personalised vehicles). The text states it comes into force with effect from 23-03-2026; effective_date left null pending legal review. Gazette print not obtained. Title, number, department and date were read from the document (09-11-2026); this is not legal verification. Scope checked against the PDF (09-11-2026): deletes column No. 8 of the Seventh Schedule and its entries (additional 2% on second or more personalized vehicles up to 10 seats owned by an individual, at registration of new vehicles only). Para 4: in force with effect from 23-03-2026.", "location": "goir/2026TRB_Ms16.pdf#page=1 .. goir/2026TRB_Ms16.pdf#page=2", "provision_id": "SEVENTH SCHEDULE", "document_type": "G.O."}, "embedding": [0.005481608211994171, 0.0014333255821838975, -0.17557671666145325, -0.0271927397698164, 0.017942672595381737, -0.03584848716855049, -0.013953465968370438, 0.02769383229315281, 0.02685256488621235, -0.014660322107374668, 0.014215216971933842, -0.016032598912715912, 0.10379360616207123, -0.025407593697309494, -0.007491912692785263, -0.04169369116425514, 0.019889606162905693, -0.05706029385328293, -0.03559546545147896, 0.025590019300580025, 0.02366125024855137, 0.04199914634227753, -0.07118561863899231, -0.029680080711841583, 0.09335293620824814, 0.010235942900180817, 0.046365659683942795, 0.02752952091395855, 0.061585213989019394, -0.013846849091351032, 0.073823943734169, -0.03472333028912544, 0.013357056304812431, -0.05322397127747536, -0.04646043851971626, -0.08125660568475723, 0.0819501131772995, 0.018827488645911217, -0.04208774492144585, -0.04266569763422012, 0.1164836585521698, -0.027184953913092613, -0.015600291080772877, -0.05288127064704895, 0.047480203211307526, -0.060274381190538406, 0.10947148501873016, 0.017491044476628304, 0.031754687428474426, 0.0002186438796343282, 0.013052713125944138, -0.021446797996759415, -0.0302573274821043, -0.03629276